// 08 TRACE SHADOW RAYS - NOT IMPLEMENTED. Stub.
//
// A placeholder so that every box of the PBR wavefront figure has a file on disk. Registered in
// src/rt_kernels.cpp with `implemented = false`, so the scheduler never dispatches it and the
// Raytracer Shaders panel greys the slot out.
//
// WHAT IT WOULD DO. Drain CRT_QUEUE_SHADOW, which a light-sampling variant of kernel 06 (and
// later 07) fills with one shadow ray per scattering event. Trace each one as an ANY-hit query
// against the same scene kernel 02 traverses - the first hit inside [tMin, tMax] is enough, no
// closest hit and no attributes - and, for a ray that reaches its light unoccluded, add the
// light's contribution to the path's radiance slot.
//
// It is the one kernel here that shares kernel 02's traversal but not its contract: it wants an
// occlusion predicate rather than a TraceHit, so crt_traverse.glsl would gain a second entry
// point (`bool occluded(...)`) that each strategy file supplies alongside traceScene(). Doing it
// that way keeps "swap the traversal" working for shadow rays too, which is the whole reason to
// write it as a contract rather than a function.
//
// See docs/plans/shadow-rays-nee.md.

#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require
#include "include/crt_common.glsl"

layout (local_size_x = CRT_WORKGROUP) in;

